h a mediocre hand\n2. See if opponent has something worth betting\n3. Potentially win at showdown if opponent also checks with a weak hand\n\nReason: With only a pair of 7s on a board showing A-J-7-7-5, my hand is very weak. My opponent has called two streets of betting, indicating some strength. Checking allows me to reach showdown cheaply and potentially win if opponent also has a weak hand, while avoiding building a large pot with an inferior holding.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
